  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043932/assets/b29bf5d439b638bfe8ab3fd013467cab8ef7c393a1cd1cf06461fa5807b6c0ba.png)\n\nFind the $x$-coordinates of the points where the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=25$ intersects the line $y=-x+1$ (sketched above).",
  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-coordinates of the intersection points, we substitute $y=-x+1$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(-x+1-1)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(-x)^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1+{x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-2x-24 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x+3)(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
